From: =?UTF-8?q?=E7=A7=8B=E5=85=83=E6=82=A0=E5=90=BE?= <goolay002@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:11:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Front page from the Home Page project: News Site hands itself
 to the portal in the Home Page folder as the app "news" (its sites.toml lists
 the sites, CoreLab under /infra among them), the supervised server restarts
 when that code changes, and without the folder "/" goes straight to News Site

The portal (routing, the list page, serving folder sites such as CoreLab) moved to
~/Documents/Claude/Home Page (HOME_PAGE_DIR overrides), so a site is added there by
editing sites.toml, without a change here. newsreader/portal now only loads its
homepage package (contract homepage.API == 1), passes News Site with its preview
(the stories several outlets carried, and the collection badge), keeps the old
addresses (/a/123 -> /news/a/123, /relay/ answered in place), and marks the public
(Funnel) name https with HSTS and noindex for every site on it. A missing, broken or
different Home Page leaves News Site served alone: "/" redirects to /news/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
